  "text": "Hermod, the Spirit of War\n\nIntroduction\nHermod is a lieutenant of Rasial, the First Necromancer. He is a phantom born out of the unending conflicts of the God Wars in the Third Age, and continuously reforms himself when destroyed as long as wars are waged on Gielinor. You can only damage him with the Necromancy combat style and poison.\n​\nIn order to fight Hermod you must complete The Spirit of War quest.\n​\nNotable drops:\n⬥  Hermodic plates, which are used for the Necromancy power armour.\n⬥  Animated drumsticks, which are used for That Old Black Magic quest.\n​\nUseful Items & Unlocks\nThese are all highly recommended.\n⬥  Undead Slayer Ability\n⬥  Undead Slayer Perk\n⬥  Salve Amulet (e)\n​\nPresets and Relics\n⬥ T90 Necromancy\n⬥ T95 Necromancy\n​\n​\n\nMechanics\nHe will only attack with Necromancy and only has 2 mechanics that differ from autos.\n⬥ Smash\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• When he does this he will draw back his sword and hit your current location. This will disable your protection prayers. When he's about to do it there will be a green aura around the location. Simply move or use  and tank it to deal extra damage.\n⬥ Conjure\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Roughly every 48 seconds he will summon 2 armoured phantoms and become completely immune to damage until they are dead. If you get this mechanic utilise  and good abilities such as  + .\n​\nRotations\nThere are currently 2 rotations which are used.\nBoth of which require  / , however for the level 76+ one you can get away without and just remove  from the rotation and just do more  spam. Equip  to dismiss your conjures.\n​\nNote: if  is not owned, add   /  at the end if needed\n​\nLevel 76-99 Rotation\n →  → enter instance →  +  →  → (tc) +  +  →  →  →  +  →  +  →  →  →  →  →  →  →  →  → \nLevel 99+ Rotation\n → enter instance →  →  → (tc) →  +  →  → build until 100 adren →  +  →  →  +  →  →  →  →   → \n​\nAFK Strategy\nA full guide on how to AFK Hermod is available here: #unknown-channel\n      \n    ",
  "normalizedText": "Hermod, the Spirit of War Introduction Hermod is a lieutenant of Rasial, the First Necromancer. He is a phantom born out of the unending conflicts of the God Wars in the Third Age, and continuously reforms himself when destroyed as long as wars are waged on Gielinor. You can only damage him with the Necromancy combat style and poison. ​ In order to fight Hermod you must complete The Spirit of War quest. ​ Notable drops: ⬥ Hermodic plates, which are used for the Necromancy power armour. ⬥ Animated drumsticks, which are used for That Old Black Magic quest. ​ Useful Items & Unlocks These are all highly recommended. ⬥ Undead Slayer Ability ⬥ Undead Slayer Perk ⬥ Salve Amulet (e) ​ Presets and Relics ⬥ T90 Necromancy ⬥ T95 Necromancy ​ ​ Mechanics He will only attack with Necromancy and only has 2 mechanics that differ from autos. ⬥ Smash ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• When he does this he will draw back his sword and hit your current location. This will disable your protection prayers. When he's about to do it there will be a green aura around the location. Simply move or use and tank it to deal extra damage. ⬥ Conjure ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Roughly every 48 seconds he will summon 2 armoured phantoms and become completely immune to damage until they are dead. If you get this mechanic utilise and good abilities such as + . ​ Rotations There are currently 2 rotations which are used. Both of which require / , however for the level 76+ one you can get away without and just remove from the rotation and just do more spam. Equip to dismiss your conjures. ​ Note: if is not owned, add / at the end if needed ​ Level 76-99 Rotation → → enter instance → + → → (tc) + + → → → + → + → → → → → → → → → Level 99+ Rotation → enter instance → → → (tc) → + → → build until 100 adren → + → → + → → → → → ​ AFK Strategy A full guide on how to AFK Hermod is available here: #unknown-channel",
